## Bandit Level 6  → Level 7

**Challenge:** 
The password for the next level is stored somewhere on the server and has all of the following properties:

owned by user bandit7
owned by group bandit6
33 bytes in size

**Solution:**
bandit6@bandit:/$ find -type f -user bandit7 -group bandit6 -size 33c -exec cat {} \; 2>/dev/null
morbNTDkSW6jIlUc0ymOdMaLnOlFVAaj


**Explanation:**
Using the find command I can again filter results for the result that I want using the find command and inputting the properties.
-user for the user that it is owned by
-group for the group it is owned by
-size for what sized file I am looking for 
since I do not have access to a lot of files i also used the stderror command 2>/dev/null to filter out all the permission denied results and to cleanly give me the password.

**Password:** [password here]
morbNTDkSW6jIlUc0ymOdMaLnOlFVAaj

**What I learned:**
using the stderr redirects the errors and discards them to give me my result.
